 a massive stimulus package he's  tax plan paid off  for today's progressives this precedent  in history could give us a way out  when tool governments have in their  toolbox to finance their actions in  addition to taxation  is that in normal times all european  countries can issue  bonds to borrow money on the financial  markets but at some point  those countries will have to reimburse  the money if financial markets trust  your country  they will lend money easily at low  interest rates  plus  but for other countries that don't look  quite as stable interest rates can rise  has a tremendous impact on the country's  ability to restore its economic strength  what might seem like a pretty  insignificant rise in interest rates can  quite quickly turn into billions of  euros to be paid back  sq control notice  in order to avoid this competition  between states and make sure we have a  truly solidarity-based recovery  progressives in the european parliament  but the idea of issuing corona bonds at  the european level on the table  in other words a common european debt  check capacity  [Music]  if the eu jointly borrows money on the  financial markets  it also needs to be able to jointly pay  back money borrowed  the progressives are pushing to create  new owned resources for the eu budget  to create independent revenue for the eu  asking for a fee on unrecycled plastics  drawing resources from the european  emissions trade system  raising income taxes on big corporates  creating a digital services tax  putting in place a tax on financial  transactions while making sure the  revenues from tax avoidance and tax  evasion go where the money is needed  [Music]  a few weeks into confinement people woke  up to a world  where the air was clean and where  traffic wasn't a nuisance anymore  spectacular drops in co2 emissions were  observed  but this doesn't give us the bigger  picture  in the last year co2 emissions have  risen more rapidly than in the 60s and  70s  from 0.8 units to 2.8 per year  temperatures continue to rise everywhere  and with it our need  to deal with the situation  [Music]  so how do we do it how do we protect  citizens jobs and livelihoods  while addressing the biggest challenge  humanity has probably  ever had to face for the socialists and  democrats  the path is clear it's called the green  new deal  with a just transition at its heart to  ensure that no one is left behind  when we rebuild our academies and our  societies on a sustainable basis  in the end progressive ideas caught the  commission's ear and by the end of  may it proposed a comprehensive recovery  plan 750 billion euros to support the  blocks economies  these investments would come on top of  an existing 1.1 trillion euro wide  budgetary plan  the hardest hit sectors in the most  affected regions must be provided with a  lifeline  to ensure they don't have to fight  workers or close down before recovery  kicks in  the snd group will continue putting  pressure on eu leaders  so that europe can live up to its  ambitions  european with the coronavirus crisis  we've all been left in a state of shock  first and foremost  was protecting people's health  supporting the most vulnerable in  society  and ensuring that workers will have a  job to return  to after the end of the outbreak but  then we also woke up to a new world of  possibilities  working from home experimenting new  forms of solidarity  and when the clapping stops and when bit  by bit that sense of normality  comes back into our lives what will we  do  will we go back to our old ways or will  we embrace  real change in this crisis the  progressives will have fought and pushed  for a real change  refusing to sit on the sidewalk of  history while watching workers  businesses and our planet go bust now it  is time to be bold and  innovative and build a better future for  all  stay tuned for next episode of what's  left where we will explore in more depth  how tomorrow's world could look like
 

